update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'For all hours in which NOx lb/mmBtu data are substituted, I certify that the  add on NOx emission controls (steam injection) were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-11D0C7BF9E1B434497408F26B0F483F0' and Rpt_Period_Id = 98 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'For all hours in which NOx lb/mmBtu data are substituted, I certify that the  add on NOx emission controls (steam injection) were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.

Jackson Generating Station Unit 7EA (or LM1, LM2, LM3, LM4, LM5 or LM6, as appropriate) is a combined cycle combustion turbine, with duct burner, where both the combustion turbine and duct burner are fired exclusively with pipeline natural gas (PNG).  During recent efforts to update the CEMS Quality Assurance (QA) and Quality Control (QC) Plan, as well as reviews of EPA Part 75 Petition Responses, it has been discovered that the existing method of determining the gross calorific value (GCV) of the PNG does not conform to the requirements of 40 CFR Part 75, Appendix D, Section 2.3.4.1.  Specifically, the GCV values are being determined on an hourly basis using an online gas chromatograph (GC), and the hourly samples obtained during each calendar month are not first being averaged before determining the hourly heat input (i.e., the hourly GCV values are used directly when determining hourly heat input).  The current situation is similar to that described in a March 14, 2014 EPA Petition Response (Re:  Petition to Use Continuous Gross Calorific Value Analysis at the Rhode Island State Energy Center, LP (Facility ID (ORISPL) 55107), except that the fuel supplier operates and maintains the online GC and then provides the hourly data to the plant via an electronic signal.  Jackson Generating Station intends to submit a Part 75 petition to continue using the hourly GCV values, and will continue the current practice of using hourly GCVs while we work through this matter with the EPA (unless directed otherwise by the EPA)' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-11D0C7BF9E1B434497408F26B0F483F0' and Rpt_Period_Id = 99 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'For all hours in which NOx lb/mmBtu data are substituted, I certify that the  add on NOx emission controls (steam injection) were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.

Jackson Generating Station Unit 7EA (or LM1, LM2, LM3, LM4, LM5 or LM6, as appropriate) is a combined cycle combustion turbine, with duct burner, where both the combustion turbine and duct burner are fired exclusively with pipeline natural gas (PNG).  The GCV values are currently being determined on an hourly basis using an online gas chromatograph (GC), and the hourly samples obtained during each calendar month are not first being averaged before determining the hourly heat input (i.e., the hourly GCV values are used directly when determining hourly heat input).  The current situation is similar to that described in a March 14, 2014 EPA Petition Response (Re:  Petition to Use Continuous Gross Calorific Value Analysis at the Rhode Island State Energy Center, LP (Facility ID (ORISPL) 55107), except that the fuel supplier operates and maintains the online GC and then provides the hourly data to the plant via an electronic signal.  Jackson Generating Station submitted a petition dated December 8, 2017 to allow the continued use of hourly GCV values, and will continue the current practice of using hourly GCVs while we work through this matter with the EPA(unless otherwise directed by the EPA)' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-11D0C7BF9E1B434497408F26B0F483F0' and Rpt_Period_Id = 100 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'For all hours in which NOx lb/mmBtu data are substituted, I certify that the add-on NOx emission controls (i.e., steam injection) were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.

Jackson Generating Station Units 7EA, LM1, LM2, LM3, LM4, LM5 and LM6 are combined cycle combustion turbines, with duct burners, where both the combustion turbine and duct burner are fired exclusively with pipeline natural gas (PNG).  The GCV values are currently being determined on an hourly basis using an online gas chromatograph (GC), and the hourly samples obtained during each calendar month are not first being averaged before determining the hourly heat input (i.e., the hourly GCV values are used directly when determining hourly heat input).  The current situation is similar to that described in a March 14, 2014 EPA Petition Response (Re:  Petition to Use Continuous Gross Calorific Value Analysis at the Rhode Island State Energy Center, LP (Facility ID (ORISPL) 55107), except that the fuel supplier operates and maintains the online GC and then provides the hourly data to the plant via an electronic signal.  Jackson Generating Station submitted a petition dated December 8, 2017 to allow the continued use of hourly GCV values, and will continue the current practice of using hourly GCVs while we work through this matter with the EPA (unless directed otherwise by the EPA).' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-11D0C7BF9E1B434497408F26B0F483F0' and Rpt_Period_Id = 101 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
