On March 31, 2022, the United States Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) approved a Jackson Generating Station petition to use natural gas hourly gross calorific values (GCVs) in lieu of monthly average GCV values.  As a condition of the approval, EPA stipulated that if at least one valid GCV measurement is obtained in a given month, each hour of missing GCV must be substituted based upon the average of the GCV values from the hour before (HB) and after (HA) the missing data incident.  However, there is no associated HB/HA sample type code available in the current reporting format.  Per guidance from Mr. Chris Worley of EPA, we have continued to report a GCV sample type code of 00 for such hours, and provide the following list where the hourly GCV was missing and HB/HA missing data substitution was applied  (22 Hours):  10/13/2022, Hr 22:00; 10/26/2022, Hr 08:00; 12/13/2022, Hrs 06:00, 07:00, 08:00, 09:00, 14:00, 15:00, 16:00, 17:00, 18:00, 19:00, 20:00, 21:00, 22:00, 23:00; 12/14/2022, Hrs 06:00, 07:00, 08:00, 09:00, 10:00, 11:00.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-11D0C7BF9E1B434497408F26B0F483F0' and Rpt_Period_Id = 120 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'For all hours in which NOx lb/mmBtu data are substituted, I certify that the add-on NOx emission controls (i.e., steam injection) were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.

