update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The XML emission file schema does not allow the reporting of Hg sorbent trap breakthrough greater than 999.9 percent. During the period of 12/19/2015 02:00 through 12/21/2015 04:00 the percent breakthrough for the trap in monitoring system 281 component ID 2TC was 1546.9. This trap failed the 12B QA criteria. The1546.9 value caused a FATAL XML Schema error when attempting to import the file into ECMPS. The import failed.
In an email, dated 1/22/2016 1:44 p.m.- reference PQA Request Tracker #46791, ECMPS support advised that, after discussion with EPA, the record should not be reported since it is a failed sorbent trap. EMSG requested a solution that would allow the reporting of that failed sorbent trap record. In an email dated 1/26/2016 1:06 p.m.- reference PQA Request Tracker #46791 ECMPS support advised to either not report the record in the XML file and add details of the omitted record in the comments section or report the value as 999.9% and add details to the comment section.
Per the recommendation of ECMPS support the record will be submitted with a substituted value of 999.0% rather than the correct value of 1546.9%.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-125CA0B4EA874A28A90715F77CFFBF3F' and Rpt_Period_Id = 92 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
