With the exception of 05/09/14, Hours 15-16 and 05/12/14, Hours 07-08, for all hours in which NOx lb/mmBtu data are substituted, I certify that the add-on NOx emission controls (i.e., SCR) were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions. For the missing data which occurred 05/09/14, Hours 15-16 and 05/12/14, Hours 07-08, the NOx add-on controls were not in continuous service based upon the associated parametric data.  Specifically, MS3A was in service for 60 minutes during each of these hours, and the time frames during which the NOx add-on controls were documented to be operating properly were as follows:  05/09/14, 15:00-15:22; 05/12/14, 7:00-7:49; 05/12/14, 08:13-08:59.  For each of 05/09/14, Hours 15-16 and 05/12/14, Hours 07-08, the NOx missing data was substituted using the Default Maximum NOx Emission Rate value in order to prevent any possible under-reporting of emission during those hours where the NOx add-on controls were not in continuous service.  Consumers Energy intends to seek US EPA Clean Air Markets Division (CAMD) guidance regarding the proper missing data substitution procedures for hours where the add-on controls are not in continuous service and may handle such events differently in the future.

' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-2235A158E60B41EEAD538B04D92D1AAC' and Rpt_Period_Id = 86 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
