On 12/03/14, the Duct 3A probe critical orifice was replaced with a critical orifice of the same size, and passing probationary calibration error (PCE) tests were then completed in Hour 15 on 12/03/14.  Additional passing daily calibration error tests were completed on 12/04/14 and 12/05/14, and the associated diagnostic linearity test was completed on 12/05/14, Hour 15.  Shortly after the PCE test on 12/03/14, the SO2 concentrations for Duct 3A appeared to be unreasonably low compared to SO2 concentrations just before the probe maintenance and concurrent SO2 concentrations observed for Duct 3B.  The SO2 concentrations returned to expected levels by Hour 00 on 12/04/14 without any corrective maintenance.  During this timeframe, the NOx and CO2 concentrations for Duct 3A looked normal.  As a conservative measure, Consumers Energy has invalidated the Duct 3A SO2 data between 12/03/14, Hr 15 and 12/03/14, Hr 23 in order to prevent the underreporting of emissions, despite all quality assurance tests having been passed.

