For the period 07/01/2016, Hour 00 thru 08/31/2016, Hour 13, flow data is based upon redundant backup flow monitoring system 341, consistent with the following guidance in the 10/05/2016 e-mail from Mr. Robert Vollaro of the EPA?s Clean Air Markets Division:  ?Here is a recommended solution.  If we allow them to replace the suspect CO2 and O2 data for the low load RATAs, then system BK1 would pass the first RATA attempt at high and low load, and met the RA specification for the 3 mid load runs.  On this basis, we could regard the first RATA attempt for system BK1 as a ?non-test?, not to be reported because mid load was not completed---and since the system did not fail at any load level and passed the follow-up 3-load RATA, there would be no loss of conditional data for system BK1.  So?.the company could report the data recorded by system BK1 as quality-assured from the start of CDV until the follow-up 3-load RATA was passed.  If we agree that this is a reasonable solution, J H Campbell would apply the final, adjusted K factors retrospectively to the data from system BK1 during that time period.  The other two flow rate systems could not be used to report quality-assured data until they passed the follow-up 3-load RATA.  The primary system would have to be used once it completed its certification.?

