update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '4th Quarter 2015 Emissions Data Qualification for Dan E. Karn Unit 2
In accordance with 40 CFR 75.34, I certify that the D. E. Karn Unit 2 SCR was operating properly during the NOx missing data periods on 11/09/15, 11/12/15, 11/15/15, 11/19/15 and 12/08/15 and that D. E. Karn Unit 2 SDA was operating properly during the SO2 missing data period on 11/12/15, 11/15/15, 11/19/15, 12/08/15 and 12/15/15.

Consumer Energy routinely runs CO2 control charts per EPA guidance, and for Load Range 09, there was a marked downward shift in CO2 concentrations starting in late September/early October of 2015 (with daily average CO2 concentrations consistently more than three standard deviations below the baseline mean).  After investigating this matter, it has been concluded that through 11/11/15, there was air in-leakage into the boiler flue gas path, upstream of all CEMS, due to a broken flapper at the bottom of the Unit 2 spray dryer absorber (SDA).  However, between 11/12/15 and 12/08/15, Consumers Energy believes it is likely that Unit 2 experienced a probe leak that may have led to an under-reporting of emissions.  Rather than invalidate the impacted data, Consumers Energy intends to submit a petition to the EPA in the near future to request an upwards adjustment of the data in lieu of standard missing data substitution regimes.  Once this matter has been resolved, Consumers Energy will adjust the data as appropriate and resubmit the 4th quarter of 2015 Electronic Data Report.

The Environmental Systems Corporation (ESC) DAHS software is not properly entering a MODC of ?21? for those hours when a value of zero is being reported in lieu of a negative value.  Consumers Energy continues to work with ESC in resolving this issue, but a DAHS software patch is not currently available.  Manually changing the MODCs to 21, where appropriate, has historically caused other calculation errors within the EDRs.  Therefore, this EDR does not contain any MODCs of 21.  The following are lists of individual hours that currently contain an MODC of 01 but should contain an MODC of 21.

SO2 Concentration (1 Hour):  11/10/2015, Hr 08:00
