update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd Quarter 2016 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 2- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  During recent limited periods of operation for Units 2 ? 4, the DataLink? program has failed to properly capture unit operating information and/or fuel usage.  Troubleshooting of the DataLink? program was performed during planned Units 2 ? 4 operating periods on August 23, 2016.  By the conclusion of the planned unit runs, the DataLink? program appeared to once again be operational.  However, in comparing 3rd Quarter 2016 DataLink? information against other internal sources of operating information, it appears as though there were errors in logging unit operating data prior to the conclusion of troubleshooting.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-33AA6C658CFC490B884001903F0AA458' and Rpt_Period_Id = 95 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '1st Quarter 2017 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Unit 4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 2- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the first quarter of 2017 indicates that Units 2 - 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Unit 4 operated during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Unit 4 did operate during the first quarter of 2017, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating data or fuel flow data for unit 4.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of this unit consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour for unit 4 has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
