update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2018 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Unit 4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Unit 4 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2018 indicates that Unit 4 only operated for two (2) hours during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicates that Unit 4 operated more than reflected in DataLink?.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Unit 4 operated more than two hours during the 2nd quarter of 2018, but the DataLink? program failed to collect unit operating data for all operating periods. Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of this unit consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour for Unit 4 has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.

