Data Qualifications:
     Two separate QA Certification events occurred during 3rd quarter for Cobb 5: one beginning on 7/14/10 and the other beginning on 8/16/10.  Both events are the result of troubleshooting the Unit 5 dilution probe to rule out a possible probe air in-leakage in relation to CO2 trends observed from the Control Chart Methodology; a subsequent probe and critical orifice replacement (same probe length, location and dilution ratio) initiated the first event, followed by a reinsertion of the old critical orifice to begin the second event.  After completion of troubleshooting and further study of control system data for the time periods shown on the control charts, we believe the outliers observed for this unit were the result of operational influences rather than sampling system in-leakage.

As will be noted from a review of the third quarter report, a substantial amount of the data has been substituted in relation to these events.  While we believe the data originally collected by the CEMS were good,  accurate data, a failure to complete the necessary diagnostic testing within the time period stipulated in 75.20(b)(3)(iv) has resulted in the substituted data.
                                
The Unadjusted Hourly Value reported in the MHV record for NOXC is in excess of the Maximum Potential Concentration (MPC) listed in the Monitoring Plan. The NOX concentrations exceeded the MPC on 08/12/10, hours 07:00 and 08:00. These exceedances were attributed to boiler control problems due to a temporary higher percentage of Eastern coal being burned in the unit due to a conveyor malfunction in fuel handling.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-47FBCB6360624A19B674BDE1A58328F2' and Rpt_Period_Id = 71 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
