    The 1st quarter 2013 EDR reflects a calibration gas cylinder with an ID number of XC034533B.  This cylinder was used for the high gas level linearity test and for daily calibration error tests starting on February 18, 2013.  When internally reviewing a draft version of the 1st quarter 2013 EDR, it was discovered that the cylinder ID number had been incorrectly entered into the data acquisition and handling system (DAHS) as XC034533 instead of the correct value of XC034533B.  While this error was corrected within the 1st quarter 2013 EDR, we note that this calibration gas cylinder was also used for the Unit 5 high gas level linearity tests during the 3rd and 4th quarters of 2012.  Unless directed to do so by the EPA, we do not intend to revise the 3rd and 4th quarter of 2012 QA XML files to update the cylinder ID number for the high gas level linearity test records.

