update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2013 Emissions Report Submittal Statement BC Cobb Plant Oris Code 1695 Unit 5

Data Qualifications: On 5/7/13, a NOx analyzer span change was completed for Cobb 5, with a probationary calibration error test completed during the 10:00 hour.  The magnitude of the Cobb 5 NOx span change was such that the historic calibration gases were no longer suitable for use with the new span.  Due to confusion between the diagnostic test policy of EPA''s Part 75 Emissions Monitoring Policy Manual (i.e., Question 12.10 in the May 2012 Draft) and the diagnostic linearity requirement of 40 CFR 75, Appendix A Section 2.1.2.5(c) (in cases where the historic calibration gases are no longer suitable for use with the new span), only an abbreviated linearity test was performed on 5/9/13 as a follow up diagnostic test for this event.  In nearly every case when a linearity test is required for diagnostic as opposed to recertification purposes, Question 12.10 indicates that the abbreviated linearity test is acceptable in lieu of the full linearity test.  However, in hindsight, Consumers Energy recognized that span changes are not currently addressed within Question 12.10, so use of an abbreviated linearity test for diagnostic purposes following a span change is not explicitly allowed within EPA policy. A full, 3-run linearity test was not performed until 6/6/13 for quarterly QA test purposes. 

In order to clarify the QA requirements for this event and better determine validity of the data, Mr. Louis Nichols was e-mailed on 6/7/13 in regards to whether an abbreviated linearity test is acceptable for diagnostic purposes following a span change.  As of 07/12/2013, Mr. Nichols has not responded to our request for guidance.  In lieu of a determination from Mr. Nichols on the validity of the data following this event and to ensure filing of the Emissions Data Report (EDR) on time, the 2nd Quarter, 2013 report contains the original NOx data collected by the DAHS during the period in question, 5/7/13 10:00 through 6/6/13 12:00.  It should be noted that in order to accomplish this submission, a QACertEventCode of 99 and a RequiredTestCode of 99 were assigned for the event in the xml QA and Certification Data files.  Otherwise, the ECMPS Client Tool would have prevented submission to the EPA mainframe (i.e., an Event Code of 170 ?Change to the Span Value of a Gas Monitor? leads to a critical error unless it is coupled with a Test Code of 09 ?Linearity Checks?).  It should also be noted that during the period in question, and shortly after the Cobb 5 NOx analyzer range change, all daily calibrations, two single run linearity tests and a Relative Accuracy Test Audit (RATA) were completed successfully for the NOx monitoring system.  In the event that the data is determined to be invalid due to QA diagnostic testing requirements, data substitution will be performed on the Cobb 5 NOx lb/mmBtu data for the 429 operating hours affected by this event, and the 2nd Quarter 2013 EDR will be resubmitted.  Additionally, the QA and Certification Data file will be resubmitted if needed with the required QACertEventCode and RequiredTestCode for the event. 
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-47FBCB6360624A19B674BDE1A58328F2' and Rpt_Period_Id = 82 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd Quarter 2013 Emissions and QA Report Submittal Statement for BC Cobb Plant, ORIS Code 1695, Unit 5

Unit 5?s NOx monitoring system employs a Thermo Fischer Scientific Model 42I NOx analyzer, and this analyzer measures total NOx (i.e., NO and NO2) via conversion of NO2 to NO, with the measurement principle (chemiluminescence) then detecting the NO which is present.  In recognition of the fact that the NOx analyzer measures both NO and NO2, Consumers Energy has historically used any NOx values available of the calibration gas Certificates of Analysis (COA), regardless of whether such values were listed as certified values or ?For Reference Only? values.  In late August of 2013, the US EPA released a final revised version of the Part 75 Emissions Monitoring Policy Manual, and newly added Question 9.34 states that the NOx concentration listed in a COA may only be used as the reference gas concentration if it is a certified value and the NOx analyzer measures total NOx.  Consumers Energy notes that for Cylinder ID XC018787B (Linearity Mid Gas), the NOx reference value is listed as 164.1 ppm, but this is a ?For Reference Only? NOx value listed on the COA; the certified NO concentration is 164.2 ppm.  Due to difficulties in revising the impacted EDR records, Consumers Energy has not adjusted the reference NOx gas concentration for this gas cylinder, but we have verified that using the certified NO concentration in lieu of the ?For Reference Only? NOx concentration has no impact on the pass/fail status of the linearity test.  Consumers Energy intends to implement the guidance provided within Question 9.34 of the revised Part 75 Emissions Monitoring Policy Manual starting with the 4th quarter 2013 EDR submittal.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-47FBCB6360624A19B674BDE1A58328F2' and Rpt_Period_Id = 83 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '4th Quarter 2013 Emissions Report Submittal Statement BC Cobb Plant Oris Code 1695 Unit 5
                               
Data Qualifications: On 11/12/2013 for the hours of 14:00, 15:00 and 16:00 the Hourly Load Value reported in the Hourly Operating Data record was 176mw. The Maximum Load Value reported in the Monitoring Plan is 175MW. Upon investigation of this event during the hours in question, it was determined that the Operations department was performing a high load capacity test on the unit beginning with the 12:00 hour continuing through the 18:00 hour. Being that this was a rare and abnormal occurrence, it was decided that there is no need to make an adjustment to the Maximum Hourly Load Value or the Upper Operation Boundry in the Cobb5 Monitoring Plan at this time.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-47FBCB6360624A19B674BDE1A58328F2' and Rpt_Period_Id = 84 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '1st Quarter 2014 Emissions Report Submittal Statement for BC Cobb Plant, ORIS Code 1695, Unit 5

The Environmental Systems Corporation (ESC) DAHS software is not properly entering a MODC of ?21? for those hours when a value of zero is being reported in lieu of a negative value.  Consumers Energy continues to work with ESC in resolving this issue, but a DAHS software patch is not currently available.  Manually changing the MODCs to 21, where appropriate, has historically caused other calculation errors within the EDRs.  Therefore, this EDR does not contain any MODCs of 21.  The following are lists of individual hours that currently contain an MODC of 01 but should contain an MODC of 21.

CO2 Concentration (1 Hour):  02/06/2014, Hr 20:00.

NOx Concentration (1 Hour):  02/06/2014, Hr 20:00.

SO2 Concentration:  None.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-47FBCB6360624A19B674BDE1A58328F2' and Rpt_Period_Id = 85 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
