update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '1st Quarter 2018 Emissions Data Qualification for Dan E. Karn Unit 1
Karn 1 HGT1 missing data period due to a failed heated umbilical. During the missing data period from  2/1/2018  12:00 till 3/8/2018  4:59 the Unit operated at an elevated HPAC (ACI) injection rate in order to ensure compliance with both its operating set-point and mercury emission limit. Sorbent traps were also installed to monitor Hg emissions.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-63589D6FF98D440FBBF80C8A58AA4B42' and Rpt_Period_Id = 101 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2018 Emissions Data Qualification for Dan E. Karn Unit 1
I certify that the D. E. Karn Unit 1 SDA was operating properly during SO2 missing data periods on 4/19/18 and 5/13/2018. I certify that the D. E. Karn Unit 1 SCR was operating properly during NOX missing data periods on 4/19/18, 5/08/18 and 5/13/2018. 
A section of heating element in the DE Karn Unit 1 mercury CEMS failed in February of 2018.  After repairing the heating element and numerous failed attempts to consistently pass weekly system integrity checks, the umbilical line was permanently replaced in March of 2018.  In the absence of any formal EPA diagnostic test policy for mercury CEMS, Consumers Energy reached out the local agency (Michigan Department of Environmental Quality) for guidance, and the local agency contacted EPA.  Ultimately, Ms. Robin Segall of the EPA?s Emissions Measurement Center and Mr. Louis Nichols of the EPA?s Clean Air Markets Division suggested that an elemental mercury linearity test and 3-level system integrity test with oxidized mercury should be conducted for diagnostic purposes.  The use of Code 99 for Required Test(s) on the related QA Certification Events Detail Record is meant to represent the mercury CEMS linearity and 3-level system integrity tests that were conducted for diagnostic purposes following the permanent umbilical replacement.
