update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The unit was in maintenance outage Oct 15-Dec 2, 2010.  Upon return to service unit was held at loads below 210 MW from 12/2 through 12/6.  When unit went above 210 MWs, it was apparent that the stack probe would leak.  The stack probe was repaired and diagnostic QA was performed.  A data evaluation was performed to assure data below 210 MW from 12/2 through 12/6 was valid data.    ' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-832F79B60F8A4168957DA39F6627459E' and Rpt_Period_Id = 72 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Evaluation showed an error of HOURMDV-20-F. This was caused by the Hourly CO2 being greater than the MPC (14). Upon review it was determined to leave the MPC as is since it was defined by a table in the rule and to monitor it during future submissions.
While reviewing the 2017Q4 data an error occured showing that the YTD data for CO2 and HI were incorrect. In order to correct the error, EM data for 2nd and 3rd quarter were resubmitted.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 100 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The MODC Informational error for 08/16/18 0300 is correct. Load bin 5 lacks quality assured operating data so the maximum hourly value stored in the next load bin is used for data subs.

While preparing for a 2018Q3 RATA is was identified the RATA should had been completed in Q2. Since it was identified after the grace period, data from the 721st operating hour through the last hour of the RATA was invalidated and substituted according to the rule. After submitting the EM and QA files to ECMPS is was identified the PMA did not update after the RATA completion. This prompted a recalculation of the data and resubmission. SFinley 10/25/18' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 103 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The NOXC MHV was reviewed due to the recorded high value on 11/02/8 15:00. It was deteremined a MP correction is not required at this time. SFinley 01/17/19' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 104 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Error HOURMHV-16-D indicated several hours where the unadjusted flow was greater than the MFP in the MP. A review of the entire year (2020) found 0.3% of the data was greater than the MFP. Based on this review it was determined no action is required at this time. ? SFinley 01/13/2021' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 112 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Error HOURMHV-16-D indicated two hours where the unadjusted flow was greater than the MFP in the MP. As found in 2020Q4, there is a very small percentage of the data greater than the MFP. Since a span/range analysis was completed last quarter, it was determined no action was required at this time.
Error HOURMHV-20-F indicated the CO2 conc was high during a single hour. The DAHS was found to have not applied the diluent cap to the 14.1% CO2 value. Since the default diluent cap value is 14.0, no adjustment was made to the data.  ? SFinley 04/21/2021' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 113 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The ""INFROM HOURMHV-16-D"" showed during a single hour, the stack flow rate was more than the MP maximum. It was determined that no change is required at this time due to the limited number of events. This will be reviewed in greater detail during the annual flow range review in January 2022. - SFinley 10/22/21' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 115 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'EM data indicates 48 hours during a period starting 12/14/221 21 and ending 12/18/2021 20 where the flow was greater than the MP span value of 16,800,000 SCFH. An investigation found operations had placed the flow in manual during this time and allowed it to get out of hand. Once the controls returned to automatic (coordinated control) the flow corrected itself and returned to normal. This was an abnormal occurrence, as such the span/ range will not be modified. However, an annual span/ range analysis is already scheduled to occur within the next 30 days. MP values will then be adjusted, as needed, based on this that analysis. ? SFinley 01/19/2022' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 116 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The INFORM error (HOURMHV-16-D); This is related to values in exceedance of the MP. A review of the data shows only a single hour is affected for SO2C. As such, it was determined no updates to the MP are required at this time. ? SFinley 10/14/2022' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83470EAEE2CD43BDACD6E0D597E05BBE' and Rpt_Period_Id = 119 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'A letter to Mr. Robert Vollaro, USEPA - Clean Markets Division is being sent which addresss the recent downward trend of the CO2 data.  Per the letter the recent Unit 4 CO2 control chart evaluation reflects a downward trend of the CO2 data since this year?s June 16, 2016 gas RATA. We have verified our CEMS are operating properly and the downward trend was a result of boiler tuning activities.  The letter outlines the past, current, and on-going efforts to tune the Unit 4 boiler for maintaining optimal unit performance that have impacted CO2 emissions. ' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83BD2A7AA5A54DC895CDF1FCC7C955B3' and Rpt_Period_Id = 95 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Received and informational error because a new mercury analyzer was installed and the testing crosssed two reproting quarters.  The main issue right now is that ECMPS does not track operating hours across quarter boundaries when determining the conditional data period for MATS. The new analyzer was installed in Q2, and there were operating hours after the installation. The conditional data period extended into Q3. As long as the 3-level system integrity check and Hg linearity were completed within 168 operating hours, you can ignore the message.    All tests were completed within 168 operating hours.  ECMPS Ticket 55907

' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-83BD2A7AA5A54DC895CDF1FCC7C955B3' and Rpt_Period_Id = 103 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
