update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'On Wednesday, March 17, 2010 a contractor for Ameren that was working on the PI data collection software noticed the CEM server was operating on Central Standard Time (CST).  He reset the time on the server to Daylight Savings Time.  Ameren discovered the problem on Monday and reset the time to CST.  With the approval of Bob Vollaro we invalidated hours 12 and 13 on March 17 and hour 12 on March 22 and left the data in between as valid data.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-8587A4179F174C45871E2DD74036ECF3' and Rpt_Period_Id = 69 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2013 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 1-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2013 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that all units operated briefly during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that the units  did operate during the 2nd quarter of 2013, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.  Consumers Energy expects DataLink? to be operational by the end of the 3rd quarter of 2013.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-8591F8F09EE14024A7486DC93C28C774' and Rpt_Period_Id = 82 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
