update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Gallatin 6 was unable to submit 4th quarter XML file through ECMPS due to a problem on PQA''s side.  Resubmitting 4th quarter 2008 on 4/29/09.  The following are changes made to the emission data:

This was done per guidance on PQA website.  On the blog site, dated January 27, 2009 ""Year-to-date"" Summary Values.

1st quarter (submitted flat file) = CO2 = 769.3; YTD = 769.3
2nd quarter (submitted flat file) = CO2 = 1122.0; YTD = 1891.3
3rd quarter (submitted flat file) = CO2 = 6129.4; YTD = 8020.7

When generating 4th Quarter XML, CO2 = 152.5 for quarter.  
4th quarter XML = CO2 = 151.1; YTD = 8177.2

ECMPS expected a value of QTD of 151.1; YTD = 8172.1

Changed 4th Quarter XML by hand for YTD.  Changed from 8177.2 to 8172.1 tons.

Also, changed 4th Quarter SO2.  DAHS Reported .5 tons; however, ECMPS expected .6 tons.
Changed 4th Quarter XML by hand for YTD.  Changed from .5 to .6 tons.

Lisa Smallwood' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A113EDA611FC4686982C3EDE0D246603' and Rpt_Period_Id = 64 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2012 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Unit 3 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Unit 3 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a datalogger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2012 indicates that Unit 3 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicates that Unit 3 may have operated for 16 hours during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Unit 3 did operate during the 2nd quarter of 2012, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting a revised EDR reflecting Unit 3 operation consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A1B0ED055FC44B818E45502752ECCE20' and Rpt_Period_Id = 78 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2013 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 1-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2013 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that all units operated briefly during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that the units  did operate during the 2nd quarter of 2013, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.  Consumers Energy expects DataLink? to be operational by the end of the 3rd quarter of 2013.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A1B0ED055FC44B818E45502752ECCE20' and Rpt_Period_Id = 82 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd Quarter 2013 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Unit 3 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Unit 3 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  For 3rd Quarter 2013,  DataLink? was not functional from July 1, 2013 until approximately July 25, 2013, and DataLink? did not collect any Unit 3 operating data for this period.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Unit 3 operated briefly during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Unit 3 operated for a total of five hours on July 2, 2013 (Hours 09:00 ? 13:00).
Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting Unit 3 operation consistent with Consumers Energy?s internal information sources, and the heat input for each operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.  
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A1B0ED055FC44B818E45502752ECCE20' and Rpt_Period_Id = 83 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd  Quarter 2014 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the third quarter of 2014 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Units 2, 3 and 4 may have operated briefly during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Units 2, 3 and 4 did operate during the 3rd quarter of 2014, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.

' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A1B0ED055FC44B818E45502752ECCE20' and Rpt_Period_Id = 87 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd  Quarter 2015 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the third quarter of 2015 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Units 2, 3 and 4 operated during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Units 2, 3 and 4 did operate during the 3rd quarter of 2015, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.

' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A1B0ED055FC44B818E45502752ECCE20' and Rpt_Period_Id = 91 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2016 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2016 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Units 2, 3 and 4 operated during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Units 2, 3 and 4 did operate during the 2nd quarter of 2016, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating data for units 2, 3 or 4 or fuel flow data for unit 4.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour for unit 4 has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A1B0ED055FC44B818E45502752ECCE20' and Rpt_Period_Id = 94 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd Quarter 2016 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 2- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  During recent limited periods of operation for Units 2 ? 4, the DataLink? program has failed to properly capture unit operating information and/or fuel usage.  Troubleshooting of the DataLink? program was performed during planned Units 2 ? 4 operating periods on August 23, 2016.  By the conclusion of the planned unit runs, the DataLink? program appeared to once again be operational.  However, in comparing 3rd Quarter 2016 DataLink? information against other internal sources of operating information, it appears as though there were errors in logging unit operating data prior to the conclusion of troubleshooting.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A1B0ED055FC44B818E45502752ECCE20' and Rpt_Period_Id = 95 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
