update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Report made on 01/08/2010 at 13:43:34' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A82EB12F40DC4C6CA2770845D3B14491' and Rpt_Period_Id = 68 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'On 07/21/2011, Unit 2 operated for six hours (Hours 14 thru 19) but the fuel flow meter wasn?t in service during this time; these represent the only Unit 2 operating hours for the 3rd quarter.  In accordance with Section 2.4.2.1(a) of Appendix D, the maximum potential fuel flow rate (i.e., 5,285.7 HSCFH) was multiplied by the number of affected hours (i.e., 6) to arrive at a quarterly fuel usage for Unit 2.  Please note that this missing data approach, when coupled with the LME methodology for long term fuel flow meters, results in certain reported hourly heat input rates that exceed the maximum heat input rate of the unit (i.e., 555 mmBtu/hr).  ' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 75 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2013 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 1-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2013 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that all units operated briefly during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that the units  did operate during the 2nd quarter of 2013, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.  Consumers Energy expects DataLink? to be operational by the end of the 3rd quarter of 2013.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 82 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd  Quarter 2014 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the third quarter of 2014 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Units 2, 3 and 4 may have operated briefly during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Units 2, 3 and 4 did operate during the 3rd quarter of 2014, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 87 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd  Quarter 2015 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the third quarter of 2015 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Units 2, 3 and 4 operated during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Units 2, 3 and 4 did operate during the 3rd quarter of 2015, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating or fuel flow data.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.

' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 91 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2016 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 1- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2016 indicates that Units 1- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Units 2, 3 and 4 operated during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Units 2, 3 and 4 did operate during the 2nd quarter of 2016, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating data for units 2, 3 or 4 or fuel flow data for unit 4.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour for unit 4 has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 94 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd Quarter 2016 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 2- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  During recent limited periods of operation for Units 2 ? 4, the DataLink? program has failed to properly capture unit operating information and/or fuel usage.  Troubleshooting of the DataLink? program was performed during planned Units 2 ? 4 operating periods on August 23, 2016.  By the conclusion of the planned unit runs, the DataLink? program appeared to once again be operational.  However, in comparing 3rd Quarter 2016 DataLink? information against other internal sources of operating information, it appears as though there were errors in logging unit operating data prior to the conclusion of troubleshooting.  Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 95 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd Quarter 2017 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Units 2-4 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Units 2- 4 employ the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the third quarter of 2017 indicates that Units 2- 4 did not operate during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicate that Units 2 and 4 operated during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Units 2 and 4 did operate during the 3rd quarter of 2017, but the DataLink? program did not collect any unit operating data for units 2 or 4. Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of these units consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour for units 2 and 4 has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 99 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2018 Emissions Data Qualification for Thetford Unit 2 (ORIS 1719)

Thetford Unit 2 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  The DataLink? information for the second quarter of 2018 indicates that Unit 2 only operated for two (2) hours during the quarter.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy indicates that Unit 2 operated more than reflected in DataLink?.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Unit 2 operated more than two hours during the 2nd quarter of 2018, but the DataLink? program failed to collect unit operating data for all operating periods. Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of this unit consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour for Unit 2 has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-A8E62EB707E24347827D8A13A9CF0766' and Rpt_Period_Id = 102 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
