Thetford Unit 2 employs the Low Mass Emissions (LME) Unit methodology of 40 CFR 75.19, including the use of a long term fuel flow monitoring system.  As part of this monitoring method, Consumers Energy employs a proprietary Microsoft Excel program called DataLink? which serves as a data logger and collects information regarding unit operation and fuel usage.  DataLink? failed to log any information for the fourth quarter of 2018.  However, other internal sources of information available at Consumers Energy suggests this unit did operate briefly during the quarter.  After conducting an investigation, Consumers Energy has concluded that Unit 2 did operate during the 4th quarter of 2018, but the DataLink? program failed to collect unit operating data. Therefore, we are submitting an EDR reflecting operation of this unit consistent with internal Consumers Energy information sources, and the heat input for each identified operating hour for Unit 2 has been estimated based upon the maximum rated heat input capacity for the unit.
