update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2009 Emissions Report Submittal Statement BC Cobb Plant Oris Code 1695 Unit 4                                  

On 05/26/2009 for the 16:00 hour the Hourly Load Value reported in the Monitoring Load record was 176mw. The Maximum Load Value reported in the Monitoring Plan is 175mw. Upon investigation of this event, it was determined that this was a rare occurrence and that there is not a need to make an adjustment to the Maximum Load Value in the Monitoring Plan at this time.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-B211B8852EE14FB8B8CB977F9C003587' and Rpt_Period_Id = 66 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '2nd Quarter 2011 Emissions Report Submittal Statement BC Cobb Plant Oris Code 1695 Unit 4   

The BC Cobb Plant has adopted the EPA''s suggested use of CO2 control charts for identifying possible monitoring system leaks. For the 2nd quarter 2011, the Unit 4 CO2 control chart for Load Bin 6 show approximately eight consecutive days near the end of the quarter where the daily average CO2 concentrations are above the baseline mean (established during the 30 days following the 05/17/2011 RATA) by more than three standard deviations. Consumers Energy is currently investigating this potential shift in CO2 concentrations, will take appropriate actions once our investigation is complete, including the possibility of invalidating or adjusting (via special petition) the affected data and re-submitting the 2nd quarter 2011 EDR.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-B211B8852EE14FB8B8CB977F9C003587' and Rpt_Period_Id = 74 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'DATA QUALIFICATION STATEMENT:

3rd Quarter 2011 Emissions Report Submittal Statement BC Cobb Plant Oris Code 1695 Unit 4  

This QA XML file contains a Unit 4 flow-to-load reference record for the mid operating level.  In the 2nd quarter of 2011, two loads were designated as normal for Unit 4 (i.e., both High and Mid as opposed to the historic single normal operating level of High).  It has recently come to our attention that the Unit 4 DAHS did not automatically generate flow-to-load reference records for both normal operating levels based upon the results of the May 2011 flow RATAs (i.e., such records were only generated for the High operating level).  Thus, we have manually generated a flow-to-load reference record for the Mid operating level in ECMPS and are working with our DAHS vendor to resolve this issue.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-B211B8852EE14FB8B8CB977F9C003587' and Rpt_Period_Id = 75 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
