update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '3rd Quarter 2013 Emissions and QA Report Submittal Statement for BC Cobb Plant, ORIS Code 1695, Unit 4

Unit 4?s NOx monitoring system employs a Thermo Fischer Scientific Model 42I NOx analyzer, and this analyzer measures total NOx (i.e., NO and NO2) via conversion of NO2 to NO, with the measurement principle (chemiluminescence) then detecting the NO which is present.  In recognition of the fact that the NOx analyzer measures both NO and NO2, Consumers Energy has historically used any NOx values available of the calibration gas Certificates of Analysis (COA), regardless of whether such values were listed as certified values or ?For Reference Only? values.  In late August of 2013, the US EPA released a final revised version of the Part 75 Emissions Monitoring Policy Manual, and newly added Question 9.34 states that the NOx concentration listed in a COA may only be used as the reference gas concentration if it is a certified value and the NOx analyzer measures total NOx.  Consumers Energy notes that for Cylinder ID CC54915 (Linearity Low Gas), the NOx reference value is listed as 124.9 ppm, but this is a ?For Reference Only? NOx value listed on the COA; the certified NO concentration is 124.8 ppm.  A similar situation exists for Cylinder ID XC031445B (Daily Calibration Error Test Upscale Gas, 07/01/13  thru 07/09/13), where the reference value is listed as 449.2 ppm, but this is a ?For Reference Only? NOx value listed on the COA and the certified NO concentration is 449.3 ppm.  Due to difficulties in revising the impacted EDR records, Consumers Energy has not adjusted the reference NOx gas concentration for these two gas cylinders, but we have verified that using the certified NO concentration in lieu of the ?For Reference Only? NOx concentration has no impact on the pass/fail status of the linearity test or the associated daily calibration error tests.  Consumers Energy intends to implement the guidance provided within Question 9.34 of the revised Part 75 Emissions Monitoring Policy Manual starting with the 4th quarter 2013 EDR submittal.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-B211B8852EE14FB8B8CB977F9C003587' and Rpt_Period_Id = 83 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '1st Quarter 2014 Emissions and QA Report Submittal Statement for BC Cobb Plant, ORIS Code 1695, Unit 4

Data Qualifications: On 02/04/2014 Unit 4?s Dilution Probe was temporarily replaced with a Like-Kind probe using the original Critical Orifice while the unit was offline. Unit start-up occurred on 02/07/2014 with first fires at 20:51. A Calibration Error Test along with an Abbreviated Cycle Time Test passed during the 22:00 hour. On 02/10/2014 an Abbreviated Linearity Test was passed completing all diagnostic testing. 
	On 03/07/2014 The Original Dilution Probe with a new Critical Orifice of the same size was installed while the unit was offline. Unit start-up occurred on 03/10 with first fires at 08:25. A Calibration Error Test along with an Abbreviated Cycle Time Test passed during the 09:00 hour. On 03/11/2014 an Abbreviated Linearity Test passed completing all diagnostic testing.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-B211B8852EE14FB8B8CB977F9C003587' and Rpt_Period_Id = 85 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
