update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'This unit had an extended maintenance outtage beginning in Q2 and ending on July 19.   After the outtage the CO2 readings were found to be lower than what they were at the time of the previous year''s RATA.  A control chart review of the data was performed in August.  After finding the potential deviation from the baseline, a plant technician checked the system for leaks.  None were found in the system.  To ensure that there were no leaks, and that the analyzer was functioning properly for the RATA, the vendor was brought in to check the entire system.  The analyzer was found to be functioning properly and no leaks were found during this visit.  The CEMS passed the RATA with an annual retest frequency on all parameters.  The CO2 data has remained consistent throughout the entire quarter and also into October.  No major shifts have occured in the readings after any maintenance events or QA tests so we do not believe that the lower CO2 readings are attributed to a problem in the sampling system.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-BEB11FCBFF674B5B9ECFFC07297034B8' and Rpt_Period_Id = 75 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'During fourth quarter 2012, Arapahoe Unit 4 co-fired a significant amount of natural gas as a supplement to the normal coal used.  This led to lower CO2 values in control chart evaluations than the baseline period.  After returning to more typical fuel operations , CO2 values came back in line with baseline data.  No analyzer problems or system leaks were found during the periods of lower CO2 data.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-BEB11FCBFF674B5B9ECFFC07297034B8' and Rpt_Period_Id = 80 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'During review of the quarterly data in preparation for submission it was noticed that the control charts were showing lower daily CO2 readings during Q1 than during the baseline period which occurred during Q3 2012.  After review of the data, we do not believe the lower values were due to a leak, but rather a combination of other factors.  First, the data during the baseline period appears to be biased slightly high based on the calibrations reading an average of 0.3% CO2 higher during that period than the bottle concentration.  During Q1, the average calibration was about 0.1% CO2 lower than target.  There is also difference in how this unit is dispatched from Summer to Winter.  In the summer it typically stays at a higher load and is ramped down when demand wanes.  In the winter it is kept lower and ramped up to meet peak demand.  We believe this diference in operation has a tendancy to produce lower daily average CO2 concentrations in the winter versus the summer months.  Finally, we looked for data shifts before and after the Linearity testing performed during the quarter and we did not find any.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-BEB11FCBFF674B5B9ECFFC07297034B8' and Rpt_Period_Id = 81 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'During quarterly report preparation it was noticed that the control chart for Arapahoe Unit 4 was showing low daily averages. After reviewing fuel consumption data it was determined that the low CO2 values were a result of the large quantities of natural gas that were co-fired during the quarter. Additionally on 7/25-26/2013 the CEMS technician leak checked the system and verified the dilution ratio. No problems were found.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-BEB11FCBFF674B5B9ECFFC07297034B8' and Rpt_Period_Id = 82 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
