update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'I certify that the automated Data Acquisition and Handling System (DAHS) component of each CEM system was tested and that proper computation of hourly averages for SO2, NOx, CO2, and heat input rate for each formula submitted in the monitoring plan, according to the requirements of 40 CFR Part 75, was verified.

I certify that the automated Data Acquisition and Handling System (DAHS) component of each CEM system was tested and that proper computation of the missing data substitution procedures was verified according to 40 CFR Part 75.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 65 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '40CFR75, App. A, Section 6.2 states ?Check the linearity of each SO2, NOx, CO2, and O2 monitor while the unit, or group of units for a common stack, is combusting fuel at conditions of typical stack temperature and pressure; it is not necessary for the unit to be generating electricity during this test.? 

JH Campbell Unit 1 and Unit 2 share a common stack.  JH Campbell Unit 1 began an extended outage on January, 14, 2011 and had not returned to service by either the end of the first quarter or prior to the end of the 168 common stack operating hour grace period for the quarterly linearity tests.  For that reason the 1st quarter 2011 linearity tests of the common stack NOx, SO2 and CO2 monitors were performed with only the larger of the two units operating.  Analysis of the common stack operating conditions indicates that the common stack temperatures and pressures were still generally representative of the range of temperatures and pressures that we observe for the common stack when both units are combusting fuel.  Based on this analysis and the fact that the probe is heated to a constant temperature, we believe the reported linearity test results are valid and should be accepted as reported.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 73 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '40CFR75, App. A, Section 6.2 states ?Check the linearity of each SO2, NOx, CO2, and O2 monitor while the unit, or group of units for a common stack, is combusting fuel at conditions of typical stack temperature and pressure; it is not necessary for the unit to be generating electricity during this test.? 

JH Campbell Unit 1 and Unit 2 share a common stack.  JH Campbell Unit 2 began an outage on September 30, 2011 and was offline for the entire 4th quarter 2011.  For that reason the 4th quarter 2011 linearity tests of the common stack NOx, SO2 and CO2 monitors were performed with only Unit 1 operating.  Analysis of the common stack operating conditions during the 4th quarter indicates that the common stack temperatures were still generally representative of the range of temperatures that we observe for the common stack when both units are combusting fuel.  Based on this analysis and the fact that the probe is heated to a constant temperature, we believe the reported linearity test results are valid and should be accepted as reported.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 76 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'QA Data Qualification Statement JH Campbell Unit 2 ? ORIS Code 1710

Please note that this data qualification statement pertains to the associated Quality Assurance (QA) XML file, but it is not possible to attach comments to the QA XML file.  The QA XML file contains QA Cert Event Records associated with the installation of Selective Catalytic Reduction (SCR) on JH Campbell Unit 2 (note that JH Campbell Units 1 and 2 share the common stack identified as CS0009).  Reagent (i.e., ammonia) was first injected into the SCR on 05/14/2013.  Installation of the SCR requires that a low NOx measurement scale be introduced for Unit 2.  Consistent with Question 15.6 of the Draft Part 75 Emissions Monitoring Policy Manual (May 2012) and 40 CFR 75.4(e)(2)(iv), Consumers Energy elected to continue using Unit 2?s existing certified high NOx measurement scale until 07/01/2013, hour 12, at which time a probationary calibration error (PCE) test was conducted on a new low NOx measurement scale.  Consumers Energy then completed the linearity and 7 day calibration error diagnostic tests by 07/8/2013.  The normal load RATA test was completed on 7/24/13.  Thus, use of the high NOx measurement scale following first reagent injection into the SCR was less than the allowed 60 days and all required diagnostic tests were completed within 90 days of first reagent injection.

ECMPS generated critical errors (Check Result = OOC-Event) for Unit 2 unless Consumers Energy specified a PCE test date/hour within one hour of the SCR related Cert Event date/hour in the Event Record.  However, based upon a review of Questions 15.5 and 15.6, as well as 40 CFR 75.4(e)(2)(iv), Consumers Energy does not believe that a PCE was immediately required following first reagent injection into the SCR in order to continue relying upon the high NOx measurement scale.  The PCE test for this event consists of the PCE test that we conducted for the low NOx measurement scale on 07/01/2013, hour 12, initiating the conditionally valid data period for reporting data collected on the new low scale.  Consumers Energy believes the ECMPS critical errors are inappropriate and wrongly invalidates hourly NOx data collected between 05/14/2013, hour 13 (when reagent was first injected into the SCR) and the subsequent high NOx measurement scale daily calibration error test on 05/15/2013, hour 04, Consumers Energy has listed the Event Date/Hour as 05/14/2013, hour 03 (which is one hour prior to the automatic daily calibration error test was conducted on 05/14/2013).  In fact, reagent was first injected into the Unit 2 SCR on 05/14/2013, hour 13.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 82 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'I certify that for the hours in which the Unit 2 NOx lb/mmbtu data are substituted, the add-on NOx emission controls (i.e., SCR) were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 83 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'I certify that for all hours in which data for the Unit 2 NOx system are substituted that the add-on emission controls were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.  During the missing data period for the Common Stack NOx system, the Unit 2 add-on controls were operating, but the NOx removal efficiency was believed to be substantially lower than the design removal efficiency of 85%.  Therefore, as a conservative measure, the Common Stack NOx missing data was substituted using the Maximum Potential Concentration (MPC).' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 88 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'I certify that for all hours in which data for Unit 2 and the Common Stack NOx systems are substituted that the add-on emission controls were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 92 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'I certify that for all hours in which data for the Unit 1 SO2 system and the Unit 2 NOx system are substituted that the add-on controls were operating properly and that the substitute values recorded during the quarter do not systematically underestimate emissions.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9A6BC4565B4452AAB750FE3130F6F93' and Rpt_Period_Id = 95 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'In January of 2016, Jackson Generating Station (JGS) discovered that the historic procedure of calibrating the duct burner fuel flow meters did not wholly conform to the requirements in 40 CFR Part 75, Appendix D, Section 2.1.5.  Based upon subsequent discussions with Mr. Louis Nichols and Mr. Robert Vollaro of CAMD, JGS has invalidated hourly fuel flow rate data (comprised of separate fuel flow meters on each combustion turbine and duct burner) whenever the duct burners were in service for any length of time.  Missing fuel flow rate data for such hours has been calculated as the arithmetic average of the hourly fuel flow rate measured and recorded by a certified fuel flowmeter system at the corresponding operating unit load range during the 720 operating hours preceding expiration of valid duct burner fuel flow meter calibrations' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-C9B1AD7C5F02472396B02F0726AD65C9' and Rpt_Period_Id = 73 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
