update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The Emissions Evaluation Report for the 1st quarter of 2014 contains various informational errors regarding 1) ten (10) hourly average heat input rates which exceed the currently defined maximum hourly heat input capacity of 879 mmBtu/hour as listed in the Monitoring Plan, and 2) three (3) hourly average loads which exceed the maximum load value of 73 MW as listed in the Monitoring Plan.  All such instances were associated with operation of Unit 1 during cold weather conditions in preparation for and/or during the Appendix E NOx correlation tests conducted on March 14, 2014.  Unit 1 is a simple cycle combustion turbine, and the achievable heat input and electrical output are heavily influenced by ambient conditions such as temperature and humidity (lower temperatures and/or higher humidity increase the achievable heat input and electrical output).  Unit 1 is used for peaking purposes and as such, it typically only operates during warmer weather conditions.  Thus, operation of Unit 1 at high loads during the colder weather conditions such as those experienced in March 2014 is not representative of how the unit operates.  For example, in 2012 and 2013, the maximum observed hourly heat input rate was 857.9 mmBtu/hr and the maximum output was 66 MW.  Therefore, Kalamazoo River Generating Station has concluded that updating the maximum hourly heat input capacity and maximum load values listed in the Monitoring Plan is not appropriate at this time.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-CABFA402F3DD48629C170B8DC082F42B' and Rpt_Period_Id = 85 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Conducted Baseload & reliability testing for annual capacity verification for the Balancing Authority on 5/28/15.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-CABFA402F3DD48629C170B8DC082F42B' and Rpt_Period_Id = 90 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = '11/19/15, Unit operated for collecting data for O.E.M. manufacture (G.E.) of the unit. The unit was operated at slightly higher loads than normal to collect the needed test data for G.E.?s review and performance analysis of this unit. ' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-CABFA402F3DD48629C170B8DC082F42B' and Rpt_Period_Id = 92 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
