update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Gallatin 5 was unable to submit 4th quarter XML file through ECMPS due to a problem on PQA''s side.  Resubmitting 4th quarter 2008 on 4/29/09.  The following are changes made to the emission data:

This was done per guidance on PQA website.  On the blog site, dated January 27, 2009 ""Year-to-date"" Summary Values.

1st quarter (submitted flat file) = CO2 = 296.7; YTD = 296.7
2nd quarter (submitted flat file) = CO2 = 1486.3; YTD = 1783.0
3rd quarter (submitted flat file) = CO2 = 4406.7; YTD = 6189.7

When generating 4th Quarter XML, CO2 = 152.5 for quarter.  
4th quarter XML = CO2 = 152.5; YTD = 6315.7

ECMPS expected a value of QTD of 152.5; YTD = 6342.2

Changed 4th Quarter XML by hand for YTD.  Changed from 6315.7 to 6342.2 tons.

Lisa Smallwood' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F416995B56904D1E9D909ED72F15B77D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 64 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The Unadjusted Hourly Value (UHV) of Flow in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan is under review. A review of the maximum values in the monitoring plan will be completed during the normal annual cycle in the1st quarter. There is no expected change to the FLOW MPF value since this value is representative of expected operating conditions.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 64 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The Nixon Unit 1 Boiler will under go a outage during the 2nd quarter. The flow messages received from the ECMPS feedback  will  be investigated. The Nixon Unit 1 flow will be monitored out of the outage to determine if no action is necessary or if  additional changes  are required. This should be completed by the end of the 2nd quarter 2009.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 65 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'The Unadjusted Hourly Value (UHV) of Flow in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan went under review during the March 2009 Outage. A review of thesystem showed air leakage in duct seals. The duct seals were replaced and as subsequent data shows the excess flow was corrected. There is no expected change to the FLOW MPF value since this value is representative of expected operating conditions

Ray D. Nixon unit 1 under went several recertification events during the outage. The critical orfice was reduce from a 300 to 1 to a 100 to 1 ratio and the CO2 monitors were replaced. In order for the QA certification events the critical orfice records were removed for Nox system and the CO2 since the Co2 monitori is the overriding event for those systems. This item was confirmed and discussed with Matt Boze (EPA) and Chris Worley (PQA). The conflicting entries were causing a BAF reset issue. All QA events were reported and passed succesfully.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 66 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Warning: The AdjustedHourlyValue reported in the DHV record for HI is in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan.  Sources are required to periodically (at least once annually) evaluate the appropriateness of these maximum values in the monitoring plan and make proper adjustments when necessary.  Adjustments may include the need to update Span, Default, and/or Unit Capacity values.  You should investigate the cause of these exceedances and determine whether adjustments to your monitoring systems or monitoring plan are necessary.  This was for a one hour period, and we will continue to monitor and evaluate the appropriateness of the HI maximum value.

Warning: The UnadjustedHourlyValue reported in the MHV record for FLOW is in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan.  Sources are required to periodically (at least once annually) evaluate the appropriateness of these maximum values in the monitoring plan and make proper adjustments when necessary.  Adjustments may include the need to update Span and/or Default values.  You should investigate the cause of these exceedances and determine whether adjustments to your monitoring systems or monitoring plan are necessary.  This mainly appears to have occured during an abnormal operating period and has not been occuring in prior recent reporting quarters, however we will continue to monitor and evaluate the appropriateness of this value.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 74 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Warning: The AdjustedHourlyValue reported in the MHV record for FLOW is in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan. Sources are required to periodically (at least once annually) evaluate the appropriateness of these maximum values in the monitoring plan and make proper adjustments when necessary. Adjustments may include the need to update Span and/or Default values. You should investigate the cause of these exceedances and determine whether adjustments to your monitoring systems or monitoring plan are necessary.

Flow RATA conducted during Q2 resulted in atypically high reference method results and a high BAF.  Flow RATA conducted during Q4 (11/2013) resulted in more typical results relative to historic tests, with a much smaller BAF.  High flow values for these few hours are likely due to this high BAF that was still being applied from Q2 RATA results. Hourly flow values will continue to be monitored to determine if changes to the maximum flow value in the monitoring plan are necessary. ' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 84 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'During review of Q4 data, it was discovered that an incorrect K-constant for the FLOW parameter was in the data logger. The value for this constant should have been 1.025 based on what was selected just prior to the three load flow RATA conducted in 2013, and was instead found to be 1.000. This was determined to have been caused by a data logger failure and subsequent download of a configuration file that contained a value of 1.000 for that K-constant. The data was affected starting July 1, 2014, which is the date this download happened. The data has since been corrected, and this resubmission is required to correct the emissions data, with the result of 2014 Q3 flow and mass emissions being ~2.5% higher than initially reported values.
' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 87 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Warning: The AdjustedHourlyValue reported in the DHV record for HI is in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan. Sources are required to periodically (at least once annually) evaluate the appropriateness of these maximum values in the monitoring plan and make proper adjustments when necessary. Adjustments may include the need to update Span, Default, and/or Unit Capacity values. You should investigate the cause of these exceedances and determine whether adjustments to your monitoring systems or monitoring plan are necessary.

After review of the data associated with this time period, it appears the two hours of higher heat input readings were subsequent to a rapid load change. A contributing factor is likely a high bias adjustment factor applied to flow subsequent to the previous RATA. As this is the first instance of this in a two year lookback period, no change will be made to the maximum heat input capacity listed in the monitoring plan. We will continue to monitor this data to determine if changes are necessary.   


Warning: The UnadjustedHourlyValue reported in the MHV record for FLOW is in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan. Sources are required to periodically (at least once annually) evaluate the appropriateness of these maximum values in the monitoring plan and make proper adjustments when necessary. Adjustments may include the need to update Span and/or Default values. You should investigate the cause of these exceedances and determine whether adjustments to your monitoring systems or monitoring plan are necessary.

After review of the data associated with this time period, it has been determined that the higher flow readings were caused by a draft door that was opened on the baghouse. This is an atypical event that is not representative of normal operating conditions, and no change will be made to the MPF for flow at this time.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 95 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'Warning: The AdjustedHourlyValue reported in the DHV record for HI is in excess of the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan. Sources are required to periodically (at least once annually) evaluate the appropriateness of these maximum values in the monitoring plan and make proper adjustments when necessary. Adjustments may include the need to update Span, Default, and/or Unit Capacity values. You should investigate the cause of these exceedances and determine whether adjustments to your monitoring systems or monitoring plan are necessary.

After reviewing data from 2016, there were two quarters in which heat input was above the maximum value listed in the monitoring plan, for a total of three hours. A change will be made to the monitoring plan as a result of this historical data review to modify the maximum value from 2550 MMBtu/hr to 2610 MMBtu/hr.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 96 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'There are several informational message warnings in this quarter related to DHV record for HI in excess of the MP max from 10/10 through 11/12, and one instance of the MHV for flow in excess of the MP max on 11/12. Colorado Springs Utilities had noted a flow data shift as well during this quarter since the Q2 flow RATA. In response to this, stack tester flow data was collected, a change to the flow K-constant was made, and a three load flow RATA was conducted and passed on 11/13 and 11/14. Since that time, Utiliities has not observed any data values for HI above MP max, or flow above MP max, and does not believe any changes are needed at this point to the MP. We will continue to observe data and evaluate if future changes are needed.' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F44788BA423E474983014FE2009AAE1D' and Rpt_Period_Id = 128 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
