update camdecmps.EMISSION_EVALUATION set Submission_Comment = 'In the third and fourth quarters of 2017, Big Rivers discovered areas of ductwork at Green Unit 1 with leaks of sufficient size to result in more than de minimis emissions of flue gas to the atmosphere prior to the location at which the applicable rules require monitoring of emissions of sulfur dioxide (SO2), nitrogen oxides (NOx), diluent (CO2/O2), volumetric flow, and mercury (Hg).   The first gap, in the wet limestone scrubber (FGD) outlet duct, was identified on August 10, 2017, but could not be fully repaired prior to the unit?s scheduled outage, which began on January 24, 2018.  The gap will be repaired before the unit restarts. The second gap, in the ductwork prior to the FGD, was identified on November 12, 2017, and repairs were completed on December 31, 2017.  Because some of the unintended emissions bypassed the FGD and all of the unintended emissions preceded the measurement of volumetric flow, the emissions of SO2, NOx, and CO2 mass emissions and emissions of Hg in lb/mmBtu recorded by the installed monitoring systems do not fully account for all such emissions to the atmosphere.  Big Rivers is working on engineering analyses to more fully quantify any unmonitored emissions and is fully committed to working with EPA to ensure compliance with allowance holding requirements.  Please contact Mark Bertram at (270-844-6176) with any questions.    ' where Mon_Plan_Id = 'MDC-F6E76ADDA0914AE2B36386899F199B8E' and Rpt_Period_Id = 100 and coalesce( Submission_Id, 0 ) <= 0;
